cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it using the metadata
  below, and cite Wu et al. (JSSC 2021) for the architecture it reproduces.
title: "fdv-adpll: cross-validated models and a sky130A detector for a differential-voltage-domain fractional-N DPLL"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Viduranga
    given-names: Anjana
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-27
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vidurangajka/fdv-adpll"
keywords:
  - phase-locked loop
  - fractional-N
  - digital PLL
  - behavioural modelling
  - verification
  - sky130
  - open-source silicon
abstract: >-
  Two independent behavioural models (an s-domain noise analysis and an
  event-driven simulator) of the fractional-N DPLL of Wu et al., cross-validated
  against each other and against the published measurements; a design-space
  dataset; and the phase detector specified from the model and laid out in the
  SkyWater sky130A open PDK, DRC clean and LVS matched.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Wu
        given-names: L.
      - family-names: Burger
        given-names: T.
      - family-names: Schönle
        given-names: P.
      - family-names: Huang
        given-names: Q.
    title: "A Power-Efficient Fractional-N DPLL With Phase Error Quantized in Fully Differential-Voltage Domain"
    journal: "IEEE Journal of Solid-State Circuits"
    volume: 56
    issue: 4
    start: 1254
    end: 1264
    year: 2021
